{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the son of an Israelite woman went out.</b> From where did he go out? Rabbi Levi says: from his world he went out. Rabbi Berekhyah says: from the parashah above he went out — he mocked and said: 'On the Sabbath day you arrange it' — does the king eat warm bread every day; is it perhaps cold bread of nine days, in astonishment? And the baraita says: from the court of Moses he went out, pronounced guilty. He came to pitch his tent within the camp of Dan. They said to him: what is your business here? He said to them: I am of the sons of Dan. They said to him: 'אִישׁ עַל דִּגְלוֹ בְאֹתֹת לְבֵית אֲבֹתָם' is written (Numbers 2). He entered the court of Moses and came out pronounced guilty. He arose and blasphemed. (Sifra, Leviticus 32)" "<b>The son of an Egyptian man.</b> He is the Egyptian whom Moses killed. (there)" "<b>Among the children of Israel.</b> This teaches that he converted. (Sifra)" "<b>And they fought in the camp.</b> Over the matter of the camp." "<b>And the Israelite man.</b> This is the one opposite him, who objected to him about pitching his tent."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:07.862816447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}